agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-d77e5c1/logs/A4-review-luna.log:18684:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/returns/A4-review-sol.json:84:      "detail": "A first batch may persist PENDING_OBSERVATION evidence for a restricted or incomplete SourceObservation. LiteratureBase explicitly permits a later open retry with the same observation_id, logical identity, and digest to replace that pending record with OBSERVED. The later topic batch records the new observed generation but does not update the first batch's evidence. _save_state authenticates the result without semantic validation. On the next load, _validate_item_evidence compares the historical persisted_observation_status and artifact fields to the current mutable literature record, so the old PENDING evidence conflicts with the now-OBSERVED record and makes the successfully returned state unreadable.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-d77e5c1/logs/A4-review-luna.log:18685:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/returns/A4-review-sol.json:85:      "reproduction": "Run c0->c1 with input A using a restricted observation so the result is PENDING. Run c1->c2 with input B using an OPEN SourceObservation with the same observation_id, canonical URI, pinned version, digest, and bytes. LiteratureBase upgrades the record and the second run returns IMPORTED/APPLIED. Constructing a new TopicObservationRunner or reading next_cursor then raises because the first batch says PENDING while the current literature record is OBSERVED."
