agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:2112:./agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/returns/A4-review-luna.json:53:      "reproduction": "Persist observed OBS-A for URI /a and content a and OBS-B for URI /b and content b. First process OBS-B so its key is in seen_observation_keys, then submit an input with observation_id OBS-A but URI /b and content b. The seen-key path at lines 882-898 returns DUPLICATE with OBS-A because lines 1037-1057 select the ID match. The current process persists successfully. A new runner rejects the state with 'duplicate item evidence idempotency key conflicts' at lines 2321-2327. This is deterministic durable identity drift from valid SourceObservation input, not a stale-contract or acceptance-rebinding issue. The alternate persisted-ID tests cover a non-ambiguous key match and do not cover this cross-match."
