agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:5034:{"severity":"P1","path":"matharc/v02/topic_observation.py","line":1037,"title":"OR-based persisted lookup can commit identity-drifting duplicate evidence","detail":"_persisted_observation_for_input selects candidates matching either observation_id or idempotency_key and then chooses by status and lexicographic observation_id. The two identities are not interchangeable: LiteratureBase rejects an observation_id reused for another logical source, and the state validator requires the persisted record selected for duplicate evidence to have the input idempotency key. _save_state authenticates the state but does not run the full state validator before committing it.","reproduction":"Persist observed OBS-A for URI /a and content a and OBS-B for URI /b and content b. First process OBS-B so its key is in seen_observation_keys, then submit an input with observation_id OBS-A but URI /b and content b. The seen-key path at lines 882-898 returns DUPLICATE with OBS-A because lines 1037-1057 select the ID match. The current process persists successfully. A new runner rejects the state with 'duplicate item evidence idempotency key conflicts' at lines 2321-2327. This is deterministic durable identity drift from valid SourceObservation input, not a stale-contract or acceptance-rebinding issue. The alternate persisted-ID tests cover a non-ambiguous key match and do not cover this cross-match."}
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:5035:{"severity":"P1","path":"matharc/v02/artifact_store.py","line":136,"title":"The commit can retire its only recovery journal before literature data is durable","detail":"ArtifactStore.put_bytes writes the blob and replaces it without fsyncing the blob or its containing directory, save_manifest does the same for manifest.json, and LiteratureBase._record does the same for observations.json at lines 411-417. TopicObservationRunner._save_state snapshots those files, writes and fsyncs the topic transaction/state/authentication/key files, verifies the in-memory snapshot, and then _remove_transaction retires and removes the journal at lines 2582-2591. A root-directory fsync for the topic files is not a durability barrier for the literature files or their nested directories.","reproduction":"Use the import path that writes an artifact and both literature manifests, then model power loss after the topic state, authentication, signing key, and COMMIT_INTENT/retirement directory entries are durable but before the literature blob/manifest file data and parent directories are durable. On restart the journal is gone, while the authenticated state names a literature snapshot whose files may be stale or missing; recovery has no target snapshot available and the literature/state binding fails or has already lost the imported data. The focused suite checks recovery deletion fsync calls and journal retirement, but injects no power-loss boundary around the import writes."}
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:5047:{"severity":"P1","path":"matharc/v02/topic_observation.py","line":"901-978, 2255-2281, 2546-2591","title":"A normal pending-to-observed upgrade authenticates historical evidence that the validator rejects","detail":"A first batch may persist PENDING_OBSERVATION evidence for a restricted or incomplete SourceObservation. LiteratureBase explicitly permits a later open retry with the same observation_id, logical identity, and digest to replace that pending record with OBSERVED. The later topic batch records the new observed generation but does not update the first batch's evidence. _save_state authenticates the result without semantic validation. On the next load, _validate_item_evidence compares the historical persisted_observation_status and artifact fields to the current mutable literature record, so the old PENDING evidence conflicts with the now-OBSERVED record and makes the successfully returned state unreadable.","reproduction":"Run c0->c1 with input A using a restricted observation so the result is PENDING. Run c1->c2 with input B using an OPEN SourceObservation with the same observation_id, canonical URI, pinned version, digest, and bytes. LiteratureBase upgrades the record and the second run returns IMPORTED/APPLIED. Constructing a new TopicObservationRunner or reading next_cursor then raises because the first batch says PENDING while the current literature record is OBSERVED."}
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:14335:/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n "replay_identity|manual_id_collision|a4_lock_audit|filesystem_durability|PENDING_OBSERVATION|pre-import|post-import|budget|fork|OFD|historical|cursor conflict" agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-luna.log agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log | tail -240' in /Users/vsiyo/Desktop/创业项目/AI4Math/Project/MathArc_Research
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:14337:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:11300:A code-certain validator mismatch is emerging: a documented `PENDING` literature record can be upgraded to `OBSERVED` by a later batch, but historical item evidence stores the old status and validation compares it to the current mutable record. Because `_save_state` authenticates without running semantic validation, the later batch can return successfully and leave state that the next read rejects.
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:14507:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:25242:+      "detail": "A first batch may persist PENDING_OBSERVATION evidence for a restricted or incomplete SourceObservation. LiteratureBase explicitly permits a later open retry with the same observation_id, logical identity, and digest to replace that pending record with OBSERVED. The later topic batch records the new observed generation but does not update the first batch's evidence. _save_state authenticates the result without semantic validation. On the next load, _validate_item_evidence compares the historical persisted_observation_status and artifact fields to the current mutable literature record, so the old PENDING evidence conflicts with the now-OBSERVED record and makes the successfully returned state unreadable.",
