agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:30042:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:4888:      "detail": "ArtifactStore.put_bytes writes the blob and replaces it without fsyncing the blob or its containing directory, save_manifest does the same for manifest.json, and LiteratureBase._record does the same for observations.json at lines 411-417. TopicObservationRunner._save_state snapshots those files, writes and fsyncs the topic transaction/state/authentication/key files, verifies the in-memory snapshot, and then _remove_transaction retires and removes the journal at lines 2582-2591. A root-directory fsync for the topic files is not a durability barrier for the literature files or their nested directories.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:30055:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:5003:      "detail": "A first batch may persist PENDING_OBSERVATION evidence for a restricted or incomplete SourceObservation. LiteratureBase explicitly permits a later open retry with the same observation_id, logical identity, and digest to replace that pending record with OBSERVED. The later topic batch records the new observed generation but does not update the first batch's evidence. _save_state authenticates the result without semantic validation. On the next load, _validate_item_evidence compares the historical persisted_observation_status and artifact fields to the current mutable literature record, so the old PENDING evidence conflicts with the now-OBSERVED record and makes the successfully returned state unreadable.",
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:30056:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:5004:      "reproduction": "Run c0->c1 with input A using a restricted observation so the result is PENDING. Run c1->c2 with input B using an OPEN SourceObservation with the same observation_id, canonical URI, pinned version, digest, and bytes. LiteratureBase upgrades the record and the second run returns IMPORTED/APPLIED. Constructing a new TopicObservationRunner or reading next_cursor then raises because the first batch says PENDING while the current literature record is OBSERVED."
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:30061:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:5035:{"severity":"P1","path":"matharc/v02/artifact_store.py","line":136,"title":"The commit can retire its only recovery journal before literature data is durable","detail":"ArtifactStore.put_bytes writes the blob and replaces it without fsyncing the blob or its containing directory, save_manifest does the same for manifest.json, and LiteratureBase._record does the same for observations.json at lines 411-417. TopicObservationRunner._save_state snapshots those files, writes and fsyncs the topic transaction/state/authentication/key files, verifies the in-memory snapshot, and then _remove_transaction retires and removes the journal at lines 2582-2591. A root-directory fsync for the topic files is not a durability barrier for the literature files or their nested directories.","reproduction":"Use the import path that writes an artifact and both literature manifests, then model power loss after the topic state, authentication, signing key, and COMMIT_INTENT/retirement directory entries are durable but before the literature blob/manifest file data and parent directories are durable. On restart the journal is gone, while the authenticated state names a literature snapshot whose files may be stale or missing; recovery has no target snapshot available and the literature/state binding fails or has already lost the imported data. The focused suite checks recovery deletion fsync calls and journal retirement, but injects no power-loss boundary around the import writes."}
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:30067:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:5047:{"severity":"P1","path":"matharc/v02/topic_observation.py","line":"901-978, 2255-2281, 2546-2591","title":"A normal pending-to-observed upgrade authenticates historical evidence that the validator rejects","detail":"A first batch may persist PENDING_OBSERVATION evidence for a restricted or incomplete SourceObservation. LiteratureBase explicitly permits a later open retry with the same observation_id, logical identity, and digest to replace that pending record with OBSERVED. The later topic batch records the new observed generation but does not update the first batch's evidence. _save_state authenticates the result without semantic validation. On the next load, _validate_item_evidence compares the historical persisted_observation_status and artifact fields to the current mutable literature record, so the old PENDING evidence conflicts with the now-OBSERVED record and makes the successfully returned state unreadable.","reproduction":"Run c0->c1 with input A using a restricted observation so the result is PENDING. Run c1->c2 with input B using an OPEN SourceObservation with the same observation_id, canonical URI, pinned version, digest, and bytes. LiteratureBase upgrades the record and the second run returns IMPORTED/APPLIED. Constructing a new TopicObservationRunner or reading next_cursor then raises because the first batch says PENDING while the current literature record is OBSERVED."}
