agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:30266:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:14337:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:11300:A code-certain validator mismatch is emerging: a documented `PENDING` literature record can be upgraded to `OBSERVED` by a later batch, but historical item evidence stores the old status and validation compares it to the current mutable record. Because `_save_state` authenticates without running semantic validation, the later batch can return successfully and leave state that the next read rejects.
agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:30436:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:14507:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/reviews-5e4ef52/logs/A4-review-sol.log:25242:+      "detail": "A first batch may persist PENDING_OBSERVATION evidence for a restricted or incomplete SourceObservation. LiteratureBase explicitly permits a later open retry with the same observation_id, logical identity, and digest to replace that pending record with OBSERVED. The later topic batch records the new observed generation but does not update the first batch's evidence. _save_state authenticates the result without semantic validation. On the next load, _validate_item_evidence compares the historical persisted_observation_status and artifact fields to the current mutable literature record, so the old PENDING evidence conflicts with the now-OBSERVED record and makes the successfully returned state unreadable.",
