10242:agents-results/2026-08-31/problem-intelligence-plane/evidence/a4-remediation/repair-517f44a/logs/topic-state-transaction.log:5035:{"severity":"P1","path":"matharc/v02/artifact_store.py","line":136,"title":"The commit can retire its only recovery journal before literature data is durable","detail":"ArtifactStore.put_bytes writes the blob and replaces it without fsyncing the blob or its containing directory, save_manifest does the same for manifest.json, and LiteratureBase._record does the same for observations.json at lines 411-417. TopicObservationRunner._save_state snapshots those files, writes and fsyncs the topic transaction/state/authentication/key files, verifies the in-memory snapshot, and then _remove_transaction retires and removes the journal at lines 2582-2591. A root-directory fsync for the topic files is not a durability barrier for the literature files or their nested directories.","reproduction":"Use the import path that writes an artifact and both literature manifests, then model power loss after the topic state, authentication, signing key, and COMMIT_INTENT/retirement directory entries are durable but before the literature blob/manifest file data and parent directories are durable. On restart the journal is gone, while the authenticated state names a literature snapshot whose files may be stale or missing; recovery has no target snapshot available and the literature/state binding fails or has already lost the imported data. The focused suite checks recovery deletion fsync calls and journal retirement, but injects no power-loss boundary around the import writes."}
